WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.430
- Now that you've lied to the
police, what are you gonna do?

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.840
- I'm going to Disney World.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.070
- A mom who faked her own kidnapping

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.320
and went to Disney World
is now facing fraud charges

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.760
for ripping off her employer.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.950
Bonnie Sweeten first rose to fame in 2009

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.780
when she engineered a kidnapping hoax.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:14.430
Sweeten called 911 and said that she

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:16.770
and her daughter had been
carjacked by two Black men.

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.820
She claimed to be calling

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.350
from the trunk of the kidnapper's car.

00:00:19.350 --> 00:00:21.930
This triggered a massive
manhunt, and one day later

00:00:21.930 --> 00:00:23.100
authorities found out that Sweeten

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.480
and her daughter were actually hanging out

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.480
at a luxury resort at Walt
Disney World in Orlando.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.370
Now, Sweeten eventually
was sentenced to 9 months

00:00:29.370 --> 00:00:31.680
in jail for the hoax, but
she wasn't done criming.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.780
In 2012, she stole over $1 million

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.130
while working as a paralegal.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.470
She was sentenced to 100
months in federal prison

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.303
for her crimes.

00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:40.140
Her latest problem arose
when she allegedly stole

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.820
from an excavating company
where she had worked

00:00:41.820 --> 00:00:43.590
as a bookkeeper since 2017.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.940
Sweeten allegedly stole checks

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.820
which she then fraudulently
endorsed over to herself.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.680
She's charged with two
counts of wire fraud, and

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.100
if convicted Sweeten faces a
maximum of 40 years in prison.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.230
I mean, if you can't trust
someone who has engaged

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:58.083
in decades of fraud, who can you trust?

